# One line per finding that has been reviewed and is not a credential. The fingerprint pins
# it to a single commit, file, rule and line — unlike a commit- or path-wide allowlist, which
# would also hide a real secret added there later.
#
# The dev APP_SECRET symfony/flex generated when the backend was scaffolded. It lived in
# backend/.env.dev, which shadowed the value in .env, so `make new-project` rotated .env and
# the derived project kept running dev on this one. That file is gone and new-project now
# rotates every env file defining APP_SECRET, but the string remains in the first commit.
# Purging it means rewriting every commit SHA; this repository has never been pushed, so that
# is the owner's call rather than a build step's. `git filter-repo --replace-text` does it,
# and this line then goes stale harmlessly.
fa6361f35b2f73f92081cba293f7d4d49a3878be:backend/.env.dev:generic-api-key:3

# The dev TOTP encryption key committed in backend/.env (ADR-0026). A DEV value, like
# APP_SECRET and JWT_PASSPHRASE in the same file — regenerated for production and provisioned
# from a Docker secret there. Pinned to the introducing commit: a different value at this
# line in a later commit changes the fingerprint's commit and re-fires, so a rotated real
# key is never silently covered.
7214e8589e50567749b9d1e5fa9e685a3f715a67:backend/.env:generic-api-key:72
